@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: added a `markdown` format. It uses the vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`, followed by a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown`.
+- `README.md`: documented the new option.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: 3 tests ran, all OK. This includes the existing `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown`.
+- `python -W error -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown`: output is the expected table, with no DeprecationWarning (so only the vendored API's supported keywords are used).
+- `git status`: only `README.md`, `stockreport/__main__.py` and `stockreport/report.py` changed. `vendor/` and the tests are untouched and no dependencies were added.
+
+## Not verified
+- Only the sample `inventory.csv` was tried. I did not test pipe characters in names, which would break a markdown table, or empty inventories.
